{"name":"Think Brick","hex":"#834841","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"think","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ponder, to go over in one's mind.","To have (some statement) in one's mind; to say to oneself mentally."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of thinking; consideration (of something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/think"},{"term":"brick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardened rectangular block of mud, clay etc., used for building.","Such hardened mud, clay, etc. considered collectively, as a building material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build, line, or form with bricks.","To make into bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thought","blocks":[{"text":"Thought, or thinking, is a cognitive process in which the mind considers, creates, or manipulates ideas, representations, or information. Core forms include judging, reasoning, concept formation, problem solving, and deliberation. Other processes, such as entertaining an idea, memory, or imagination, are also frequently considered types of thought. Thought may arise in response to perception, but can also occur without immediate input from the sensory organs. In a broader sense, any mental event—including perception and unconscious processes—may be described as forms of thought. The term can also denote not the process itself, but the resulting mental states or systems of ideas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Jardin_du_Musee_Rodin_Paris_Le_Penseur_20050402_%2802%29.jpg/330px-Jardin_du_Musee_Rodin_Paris_Le_Penseur_20050402_%2802%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thought"},{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg/500px-Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg/500px-Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Man thinking on a train journey","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/500px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/1280px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/500px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wall constructed in glazed-headed Flemish bond brickwork pattern, with various shades and lengths","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrick_wall_close-up_view.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg/500px-%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg/1280px-%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg?utm_source=